    "done_when": "A measurement script at docs/research/data/landing-record-merge-measure/measure.py, run from this repository, builds two arms in a scratch clone or worktree outside this checkout, both starting from base 457bbec7. The six commits are velocity 9afcdbe0, worker anatomy 11fb09a4, coordinator overhead 4413e78a, code depth 77876fa0, nova flapping e01ec2ad and nova readiness 9cf52140. The before arm takes the six as they are; the after arm rewrites each so its evidence anchor lands in its own docs/evidence/fragments/PLAN/NODE.html and its plan edit becomes a landing: line in place of a plan-file edit. The script folds each arm's six commits together with git merge-tree and counts conflicted paths under docs/plans and docs/evidence. It then runs reckon.evidence.compose_landed_record over the after arm's merged tree and counts the six anchors in the composed record. The recorded log states: the before arm's conflict count, expected above zero; the after arm's conflict count, required to be zero; the six anchor ids, each found once in the composed record; the revision; and reckon.__file__. The log is cited in the manifest with an EXIT= line. If one of the six commits cannot be found in this repository's history, the log says which, and the measure runs on the rest. Nothing outside the scratch location is modified. The node's own evidence fragment records the two counts and the anchor check, with a figure of before against after under the node's own figure directory, and the manifest carries one landing: line.",
